LAR polygon and default launch point (port of calcLARPoints/drawJDAMLAR; map-grid maths, x north, y east, angles from +x toward +y):
function larGeometry(t) { const { lar_rmin_nmi, lar_rmax_nmi, lar_half_angle_deg } = lar(t.drop_alt, t.drop_spd);
  const rMin = lar_rmin_nmi * 1852, rMax = lar_rmax_nmi * 1852, rad = (d) => d * Math.PI / 180;
  const c = rad((t.attack_heading + 180) % 360), L = c - rad(lar_half_angle_deg), R = c + rad(lar_half_angle_deg);
  const P = (r, a) => ({ x: t.x + r * Math.cos(a), y: t.y + r * Math.sin(a) }), pts = [];
  for (let i = 0; i <= 3; i++) pts.push(P(rMin, L + (R - L) / 3 * i));   // inner arc L->R (4 points)
  pts.push(P(rMax, R));                                                   // right edge
  for (let i = 5; i >= 0; i--) pts.push(P(rMax, L + (R - L) / 6 * i));   // outer arc R->L (6 points) => 11 vertices
  const mid = (rMin + rMax) / 2;
  return { lar_polygon: pts, centre: P(mid, c) }; }
Exporter: for an active target set launch_x/launch_y = user launch point if it is inside lar_polygon (ray casting), else the nearest point on the polygon edge, else (no user point) centre. Writing lar_polygon is optional (ME output contains it, setData ignores it).
